# Fork-only: per-project CI checks that prove "the tests ran".
#
# Single source of truth read by bin/fm-ci-test-checks-lib.sh, which both
# bin/fm-merge-proof-lib.sh (merge proof) and bin/fm-nm-base-skip-pretool-check.sh
# (dev-bound `--skip test`) use. Without it the merge proof could only look for
# a check named "test", and backend CI names its test jobs `unit` and
# `integration`, so a dev-bound PR that skipped the local test step could not
# merge without a waiver.
#
# Schema, one entry per line, `#` starts a comment:
#   <project> <pattern>   a CI check that must pass at the PR head
#   <project> -           the project declares no CI test check
# <project> is the GitHub repository name (the clone's name in data/projects.md).
# <pattern> is the rest of the line: an extended regex matched against the whole
# check's own job name in lower case (the rollup name, without the workflow
# name). Repeat a project to require several checks; every one must have a
# green match.
# Spaces inside a pattern are literal.
#
# What a declaration changes:
#   merge proof  a skipped local test step needs every declared check green.
#                A project that is `-` or absent keeps the old rule: any green
#                check with "test" or "tests" as a word in its name.
#   skip hook    a dev-bound run must `--skip test` only for a project with
#                declared checks. Any other project keeps the local test step,
#                so a dev-bound PR never reaches merge with no tests run.
#
# Evidence (read from each clone's .github/workflows on 2026-11-23):
#   apply_pass_backend  ci.yml runs on pull_request: jobs `unit` and `integration`
#                       (plus integration-shard (N/4), which `integration` waits for).
#   apply_pass_frontend ci.yml runs on pull_request: matrix job `test`, reported as `test (N)`.
#   ai_backend          no pull_request test check on dev: the "Lint & test" job runs only
#                       from push to dev and from PRs to main. Its .no-mistakes.yaml has
#                       no commands.test, so the local test step is the only dev-bound test.
#   applypass-infra, applypass-plugins, auto_applier_py, auto_scraper: no test workflow.
apply_pass_backend unit
apply_pass_backend integration
apply_pass_frontend test \([0-9]+\)
ai_backend -
applypass-infra -
applypass-plugins -
auto_applier_py -
auto_scraper -
